cff-version: 1.2.0
title: >-
  Analytical Modeling Scripts of Layered Composite Timber
  Beams
message: >-
  If you use these scripts in your research, please cite
  them using the metadata below.
type: software
authors:
  - given-names: Arthur
    family-names: Duyck
    email: 537278@umons.ac.be
    affiliation: >-
      University of Mons, Department of Structural
      Mechanics - Timber Research Group
identifiers:
  - type: doi
    value: 10.5281/zenodo.22826936
    description: Concept DOI (resolves to the latest version)
repository-code: 'https://github.com/REPLACE/WITH-YOUR-REPOSITORY'
abstract: >-
  Python implementations of five analytical methods for the
  mechanical modelling of layered composite timber beams
  with interlayer slip: the exact Girhammar theory for two
  layers, its generalisation to n layers, the Eurocode 5
  gamma-method (Heimeshoff), an extended matrix-based
  gamma-method for an arbitrary number of layers, and the
  Kreuzinger shear analogy method. The scripts compute
  internal forces, deflections, stresses and connector
  forces for a simply supported beam under several loading
  modes, and are intended for the comparison of these
  approaches on a common basis.
keywords:
  - timber engineering
  - composite beams
  - interlayer slip
  - partial composite action
  - gamma-method
  - shear analogy
  - Eurocode 5
